blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"The following piece of code: https://getpsalm.org/r/5766566f20\r\n\r\n```php\r\n<?php\r\n\r\n/**\r\n * @return array<int,int>\r\n */\r\nfunction foo(): array {\r\n    $foo = [\r\n        [1, 2, 3],\r\n        [1, 2],\r\n    ];\r\n\r\n    return array_intersect(... $foo);\r\n}\r\n\r\n/**\r\n * @return array<int,int>\r\n */\r\nfunction bar(): array {\r\n    $foo = [\r\n        [1, 2, 3],\r\n        [1, 2],\r\n    ];\r\n\r\n    return array_intersect($foo[0], $foo[1]);\r\n}\r\n\r\nprint_r(foo());\r\nprint_r(bar());\r\n```\r\n\r\nProduces the errors:\r\n\r\n```\r\nERROR: InvalidReturnStatement - 12:5 - The type 'array<int, array{0:int, 1:int, 2?:int}>' does not match the declared return type 'array<int, int>' for foo\r\n\r\nERROR: InvalidReturnType - 4:4 - The declared return type 'array<int, int>' for foo is incorrect, got 'array<int, array{0:int, 1:int, 2?:int}>'\r\n```\r\n\r\nEven though the functions are equivalent. Seems the type is incorrectly inferred through the splat operator.\r\n\r\n","closed_by":{"login":"muglug","id":2292638,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyOTI2Mzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2292638?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/muglug","html_url":"https://github.com/muglug","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/muglug/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/muglug/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/muglug/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/muglug/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/muglug/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/muglug/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/muglug/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/muglug/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/muglug/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false